# P15 (docs/phase15-brief.md 2.4, 6 item 12, 7): Settings > EQ walks the
# presets, hardware and software ones and Off, and every apply logs which
# engine runs it ("eq engine=hw|sw preset= maxerr= precut=", after the
# unchanged "eq preset= enabled= precut=" line). check_trace.py's p15eq
# rule checks each pair against the generated table
# (apps/ipodui/eq_hw_presets.c: every preset on hw since the owner's
# 2026-10-11 call, EQ_HW_MAXERR 255) and that exactly one engine is on: hw -> software EQ flat
# (enabled=0 precut=0), sw -> software EQ enabled, Off -> neither.
# Order of presets, the list is Off then 1..22:
#   0 Off -> 1 Acoustic (hw) -> 5 Dance (hw, worst fits) -> 2 Bass Booster (hw)
#   -> 20 Treble Booster (hw) -> 8 Flat (hw) -> 16 R&B (hw) -> 0 Off
# so hw -> sw -> Off and sw -> hw are both walked.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-p15-eq-engine.script
# trace: p15eq
# eq-engines: 0=sw 1=hw 5=hw 2=hw 20=hw 8=hw 16=hw
# log: eq engine=hw preset=1 maxerr=13 precut=8
# log: eq engine=hw preset=5 maxerr=22 precut=
# log: eq engine=sw preset=0 maxerr=0 precut=0
# golden: skip end_off

wait 4000
wheel +3             # Settings
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 1500
wheel +9             # EQ
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 1500
wheel +1 300         # Acoustic (hw)
wait 500
key SELECT
wait 800
key SELECT           # reopen: the applied preset is highlighted
wait 1200
wheel +4 300         # Dance (hw)
wait 500
key SELECT
wait 800
key SELECT
wait 1200
wheel -3 300         # Bass Booster (hw)
wait 500
key SELECT
wait 800
key SELECT
wait 1200
wheel +18 120        # Treble Booster (hw)
wait 800
key SELECT
wait 800
key SELECT
wait 1200
wheel -12 120        # Flat (hw)
wait 800
key SELECT
wait 800
key SELECT
wait 1200
wheel +8 150         # R&B (hw)
wait 800
key SELECT
wait 800
key SELECT
wait 1200
wheel -16 100        # Off
wait 800
key SELECT
wait 1200
shot end_off
quit
